#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:123
msgid "Cash disbursed or payments by implementing partner."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:126
msgid ""
"Payment rows are grouped by the programme's implementing partner using the "
"same date and status filters as the financial timeline."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:130
msgid ""
"The card appears once the financial feed provides the implementing-partner "
"dimension. Top 10 partners plus an Other bucket."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:138
msgid ""
"People reached in households with at least one qualifying payment in the "
"period."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:139
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:154
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:168
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:185
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:195
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:204
msgid "HOPE households and payments — country report demographic feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:141
msgid ""
"A household counts once per period when it has a qualifying payment. "
"Individuals, children and persons with disabilities come from the "
"household's recorded composition. Date basis: payment delivery date, then "
"entitlement date, then payment status date. Only accepted, finished or "
"closed plans are included; failed, removed, conflicted and excluded payments "
"are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:148
msgid ""
"Children and PWD figures rely on recorded household fields, so missing "
"composition or dates of birth understate the totals."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:153
msgid ""
"Children reached in households with at least one qualifying payment in the "
"period."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:156
msgid ""
"Sums each household's recorded children count (the household composition "
"count where available, otherwise the beneficiary-recorded children count). "
"Households with no recorded count contribute zero."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:161
msgid ""
"Where household composition has not been recalculated or children's dates of "
"birth are missing, the figure is understated. An improved estimate based on "
"household members is being added to the feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:167
msgid ""
"Individuals, households, children or persons with disabilities reached over "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:170
msgid ""
"Demographic rows come from households with at least one qualifying payment "
"in the month. Payment plans must be accepted, finished or closed; failed, "
"removed, conflicted and excluded payments are excluded. Households are "
"counted distinctly. Beneficiary, child and PWD counts follow the household's "
"recorded composition; missing composition or dates of birth understate the "
"totals."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:177
msgid ""
"Under the current legacy calculation, a household with more than one "
"qualifying payment in a month can contribute its size, children and PWD "
"counts once per payment; total households remains distinct. PWD figures may "
"be under-reported where programmes do not collect them."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:184
msgid "Share of the reached population by programme sector."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:187
msgid ""
"Uses the same demographic base as the reach timeline, grouped by programme "
"sector. Shares are calculated from the active metric (individuals, "
"households, children or persons with disabilities)."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:191
msgid "Children and PWD under-reporting caveats also apply here."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:194
msgid "Share of the reached population by country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:197
msgid ""
"Uses the same demographic base as the reach timeline, grouped by business "
"area country. Shares are calculated from the active metric."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:200
msgid "The chart shows the top 10 countries. Children and PWD caveats apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:203
msgid "Reached population by beneficiary group."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:206
msgid ""
"Uses the same demographic base as the reach timeline, grouped by the "
"programme's beneficiary group label. Values follow the active metric."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:209
msgid "The chart shows the top 10 groups. Children and PWD caveats apply."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:215
msgid "Reconciled and still-open payments or amount over time."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:216
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:231
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:244
msgid "HOPE payments — country report completion feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:218
msgid ""
"Reconciled includes Sent to Payment Gateway, Sent to FSP, Distribution "
"Successful, Partially Distributed and Transaction Successful. All other non-"
"failed statuses are Still open. Only payments in accepted, finished or "
"closed plans are included; failed, removed and conflicted payments are "
"excluded. USD is entitlement USD."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:224
msgid ""
"Reconciled is green and Still open is amber across the timeline and country "
"charts. The status mapping is applied when the report rows are loaded; Still "
"open includes pending and other non-reconciled statuses."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:230
msgid "Reconciled and still-open payments by country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:233
msgid ""
"Uses the same completion base as the reconciliation timeline, grouped by "
"business area country. Each bar is the stacked total of reconciled and still-"
"open values for the active metric."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:238
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Top 10 countries by total volume. Absolute values is the default; 100% share "
"shows each country's reconciled and still-open split as percentages."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:243
msgid "Reconciled payments by beneficiary group."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:246
msgid ""
"Uses the same completion base as the reconciliation timeline, grouped by the "
"programme's beneficiary group label. Values follow the active metric."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:249
msgid "The chart shows the top 10 groups."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:252
msgid "Reconciliation and delivery success rates by country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:253
msgid "HOPE payments — financial and completion feeds."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:255
msgid ""
"Reconciliation rate is reconciled divided by reconciled plus still open in "
"the completion feed. Delivery success rate is successful statuses divided by "
"successful plus pending statuses in the financial feed. Only countries "
"present in both feeds are shown."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:261
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Top 12 countries by completion volume, sorted by reconciliation rate. The "
"dashed 80% line is a reference guide, not a threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:266
msgid ""
"Payment verification outcomes: selected, verified, pending and discrepancies."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:267
msgid ""
"HOPE payments — verification records in the country report completion feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:269
msgid ""
"Counts payments by verification outcome for the selected period. The "
"completion rate is successfully verified payments divided by payments "
"selected for verification."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:272
msgid ""
"Appears once the completion feed provides verification rows (dimension type "
"verification)."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:278
msgid ""
"Grievance ticket volume over time, split into closed/resolved and open/"
"active."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:279
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:289
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:299
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:308
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:314
#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:326
msgid "HOPE grievances — country report grievance feed."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:281
msgid ""
"Counts tickets by created date. Ignored tickets are excluded and business "
"area must be set. Closed covers the Closed and Resolved statuses; Open & "
"Active covers New, Assigned, In Progress, On Hold and For Approval."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:285
msgid "HOPE integer status codes are mapped to labels before charting."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:288
msgid "Grievance tickets by status."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:290
msgid "Counts tickets by the status value for the selected period and country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:292
msgid ""
"Unknown means the source status field was blank. This doughnut is used until "
"resolution-time data is available, when it will be replaced by Average "
"Grievance Resolution Time by Category."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:298
msgid "Grievance tickets by priority."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:300
msgid ""
"Counts tickets by the priority value for the selected period and country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:302
msgid ""
"Priority is an optional field in HOPE, so many tickets have none; these are "
"reported as Not Set (source value 0)."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:307
msgid "Grievance tickets by category."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:309
msgid ""
"Counts tickets by the category value for the selected period and country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:310
msgid ""
"The chart shows the top 10 categories. Unknown means the category was blank."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:313
msgid "Grievance tickets by subcategory."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:316
msgid ""
"Counts tickets by the subcategory value (stored as issue_type in HOPE) for "
"the selected period and country."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:320
msgid ""
"The chart shows the top 10 subcategories. Unknown means the subcategory was "
"blank. HOPE calls this field Subcategory."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:325
msgid ""
"Grievance tickets by country, split into closed/resolved and open/active."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:328
msgid ""
"Uses the same ticket base as the grievance timeline, grouped by business "
"area country. Each bar is the stacked total of closed/resolved and open/"
"active tickets."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:331
msgid "The chart shows the top 10 countries by total tickets."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:338
msgid ""
"Global delivery over time: cash disbursed, payment count, and the number of "
"individuals, households and children reached by household programmes."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:341
msgid ""
"HOPE payments and household registration data, aggregated by the country "
"report."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:343
msgid ""
"Total Cash Disbursed sums delivered quantity in USD. Payments Count counts "
"payment records — not payment plans, unique recipients or only completed "
"payments. Individuals Reached sums the registered household size of reached "
"households; Households Reached counts those households; Children Reached "
"sums the children recorded in household composition. Frontline (incentive) "
"workers are reported separately and are not part of these series."
msgstr ""

#: src/hope_live/web/chart_metadata.py:351
msgid ""
"All years is the default. Last 5 years shows the current year and the "
"previous four. Selecting a year shows its monthly data. Where a year or "
"month has no demographic record, the reached series are estimated from "
"payment volume."
msgstr ""

